## Problem 8 — draining a real server

Edit `ex8/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface Drainable {
  url(): string;                       // e.g. "http://127.0.0.1:53412"
  connections(): number;
  drain(options?: { deadlineMs?: number }): Promise<"clean" | "forced">;
}

export function createDrainableServer(
  handler: (req: import("node:http").IncomingMessage, res: import("node:http").ServerResponse) => void,
): Promise<Drainable>
```

Listen on `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port), track every socket, and implement
`drain`:

1. stop accepting new connections (`server.close()`);
2. close idle keep-alive connections immediately;
3. wait for in-flight requests to finish, up to `deadlineMs` (default 1000);
4. resolve `"clean"` if everything ended in time, or destroy the remainder and
   resolve `"forced"`.

`connections()` reports how many sockets are currently open. A second `drain`
call resolves the same way as the first without doing the work twice.

```
uv run dojo test node v3nc03_cluster_scaling ex8
```

